The fonts built into Terse
==========================

terse-host draws all text with three fonts that are built into it
(include_bytes!, src/fonts.rs), so it needs no installed fonts and draws
the same on every system (SPEC.md §terminal.text, README "Fonts"):

  DejaVuSansMono.ttf   the terminal, and the page's monospace face   340,712 bytes
  DejaVuSans.ttf       the page's sans (and serif) face              757,076 bytes
  DejaVuSans-Bold.ttf  the page's bold text                          705,684 bytes
                                                            together 1,803,472 bytes

They are DejaVu fonts version 2.37, unmodified, from the project's
official release:

  https://github.com/dejavu-fonts/dejavu-fonts/releases/download/version_2_37/dejavu-fonts-ttf-2.37.tar.bz2
  sha256 fa9ca4d13871dd122f61258a80d01751d603b4d3ee14095d65453b4e846e17d7
  (downloaded 2026-11-21; the three files are ttf/ in that archive)

  sha256 of the files:
  b4a6c3e4faab8773f4ff761d56451646409f29abedd68f05d38c2df667d3c582  DejaVuSansMono.ttf
  7da195a74c55bef988d0d48f9508bd5d849425c1770dba5d7bfc6ce9ed848954  DejaVuSans.ttf
  e6476c1b80502924294eed40894c5b18e06c181444ca953e5334262df9c27724  DejaVuSans-Bold.ttf

LICENSE is the archive's LICENSE file: the Bitstream Vera fonts licence
(DejaVu's changes are in the public domain) and the Arev fonts licence.
It allows the fonts to be copied, embedded and redistributed with other
software as long as the copyright and permission notices are included;
every Terse download ships this LICENSE as FONTS-LICENSE.txt.

The fonts are shipped whole, not subset to the full repertoire: no
subsetting tool is part of the build, and the characters beyond the
repertoire (Armenian, Georgian, Hebrew, Arabic, more symbols) are drawn
too.
